========================================================================
Case-provenance credit block
========================================================================

The M1 shipping set (V01_Replay, V02_Overpayment, V03_CrossResource,
V04_DoubleGrant) reproduces four published x402 attack classes catalogued
in `coverage_map.md`:

  - arXiv:2605.11781, "Five Attacks on x402 Agentic Payment Protocol"
    (payment-authorization integrity classes ×3; settlement-race duplicate
    service grant class ×1).
  - arXiv:2605.30998, "Free-Riding the Agentic Web" (cross-class overlap
    on facilitator-side accounting).
  - arXiv:2604.11430 (PII-hardening methodology; informs the clean-twin
    baseline, not itself a reproduced twin).

The M1+ / novel-variant additions (V05_CrossDomain, V06_DelegationCap)
are class-level twins against synthesized minimal contracts; they cover
attack classes the arXiv corpus does not name and are not disclosures of
any specific live SDK. Attribution to the paper authors is preserved in
`coverage_map.md` under the per-class rows.

Reference implementation being reproduced: the Coinbase x402 reference
family and the Linux Foundation x402 Foundation working-group spec. This
repository does not vendor any x402 SDK source; the twin contracts are
minimal reference implementations authored for CI use.

